Why the data is not MIT
-----------------------

Cases and reports are reproducible measurements, not executable assets. A
derivative work (further mutated cases, a comparison report) must keep the
attribution and the provenance chain, otherwise a number can be quoted without
its measurement conditions. A copyleft licence (ShareAlike) would
unnecessarily restrict how a paper or a third-party re-evaluation may cite
them, and a proprietary licence would block reproduction altogether. CC BY 4.0
keeps them freely usable and redistributable while requiring attribution.

How to attribute
----------------

When reusing `cases/` or `reports/`, credit:

  Agent-Quality-Gate (c) 2026 xuanluo111,
  dataset epoch <dataset_epoch> (see cases/suite_manifest.json),
  licensed under CC BY 4.0.

State the dataset epoch (or the run id for a report) whenever you quote a
number: the risk ledger and pass rates are only comparable within one dataset
epoch, so an un-epoch-ed citation is not reproducible. Do not imply that the
original authors endorse any derivative conclusion.

